IO-49: date the .out header one report step before the first saved period

output_open() stores a "report start date" that readers turn into period
dates as header + (k+1)*REPORT_STEP. With REPORT_START later than START it
computed floor((ReportStart - StartDateTime)/step) - 1 steps, but the first
saved period is the first report time at or after REPORT_START (a ceil), and
the day-fraction quotient of an aligned REPORT_START is often n - 2e-10, so
the header was usually one step early. Count the whole seconds to
REPORT_START with datetime_timeDiff() and take the ceiling.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-49_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/output.c b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
index f57370e..8441a3d 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/output.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
@@ -394,7 +394,10 @@ int output_open()
     if ( StartDateTime + z > ReportStart ) z = StartDateTime;
     else
     {
-        z = floor((ReportStart - StartDateTime)/z) - 1.0;
+        // --- the first saved period is the first report time at or
+        //     after ReportStart (count whole seconds, not day fractions)
+        z = ceil(datetime_timeDiff(ReportStart, StartDateTime) /
+                 (double)ReportStep) - 1.0;
         z = StartDateTime + z*(double)ReportStep/86400.0;
     }
     fwrite(&z, sizeof(REAL8), 1, Fout.file);
